  "description": "Truncation at the other end of the scale: the whole result is discarded. 0.05 at 15.00 - the rate discgrp.txt row 0 carries verbatim for A000000000 type 01 category 0001 - has an exact quotient of 0.000625, and the store at :464-465 keeps none of it. TRAN-AMT is 0000000000{, the zoned image of a positive zero, and not 0000000000A: a rounding mode would keep a tenth of a cent the COBOL never stores, and at this magnitude that is the entire amount. Nothing about the record differs from a genuinely zero-interest one, which is exactly the point - the difference between truncating and rounding here is the difference between writing zero and writing a cent that does not exist.",
